.autoeda/runtime/results/stmap93/review_prompt1.txt
Review the uncommitted stmap93 implementation in this ABC repository for correctness and integration issues. Focus on source changes for stmap93: src/base/abci/abcStmap_93.c, src/base/abci/abc.c, src/base/abci/abcStmap_65.c, src/base/abci/module.make, abclib.dsp, and src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c. The hypothesis is a final-critical emitted-AIG drive/load target with a relaxed exact-area area-premium window only when the current best has zero area-flow bookkeeping and the candidate has materially stronger drive. Older stmap commands and map should remain gated from this behavior. Required validation already passed locally: build, stmap93 -h, i10 smoke, path normalization, unknown-network stale-state check, implementation check, full four-benchmark evaluation, and CEC 4/4. stmap93 produced two relaxed overrides on or1200 but final QoR stayed unchanged. Please report discrete bugs, stale-state leaks, command registration/build issues, unintended behavior changes for older commands, missing gates, unsafe window logic, or validation gaps.
